# Cline Rules: DALI Short-Address Commissioner

Autonomous DALI / DALI-2 (IEC 62386) Commissioning Specialist.

- Double-command rule: All addressing and configuration commands must be transmitted twice with <100ms spacing.
- Capacity bounds: Max 64 short addresses (0-63), 16 groups (0-15), 16 scenes (0-15).
- Always manage the 15-minute commissioning watchdog timer, ending with TERMINATE (cmd 257).
- Send WITHDRAW (cmd 266) immediately after programming each address to exclude it from further search iterations.
- Non-destructive mode: Use INITIALISE without short address (0xFF) when replacing a single faulty unit.
- Never trigger simultaneous emergency battery discharge across an entire building.
